# shellcheck shell=bash

# The versions of the gate's external tools. Sourced by BOTH
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (which installs them) and scripts/local-ci.sh
# (which verifies what it found matches). One file, so the two sides cannot
# name different versions.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. shellcheck and yamllint used to come from the runner's apt
# and from whatever the developer's distro shipped, so their versions were
# free to differ — and on 2026-08-18 they did. Local shellcheck 0.11.0 passed
# `scripts/*.sh`; the runner's 0.9 reported SC2015 on two lines of
# install-desktop-entry.sh and every push that day went red. "The local run
# matches GitHub exactly" was false, and nothing said so, because the two runs
# executed the same *steps* with different *tools*.
#
# Pinning the steps was never enough. A gate is its tools.
#
# TO BUMP ONE: change it here, run ./scripts/local-ci.sh, and install the same
# version locally. tests/test_ci_contract.py fails if the workflow stops
# agreeing with this file, so a half-done bump cannot reach GitHub.
#
# Format is deliberately plain `KEY=value` with no expansion, quoting or
# logic: it is sourced by bash and read by a regex in the test, and anything
# cleverer would need a parser on both sides.

# Version 0.11.0 relaxed SC2015 for `command -v` guards and 0.9 did not; that
# difference is the whole reason this file exists — see above. (Do not start a
# comment line here with the tool's own name: shellcheck reads `# <name> ...`
# as one of its directives and refuses to parse the file at all.)
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.11.0

# The checksum of the tarball that version names, because the workflow fetches
# it over the network and then executes it over the checkout — in a job that
# SHA-pins its actions for exactly that reason. A version pins WHICH artifact
# to ask for; only this pins WHAT came back.
#
# TO BUMP: change the version above, then
#   curl -fsSL -o /tmp/sc.tar.xz \
#     "https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/releases/download/vX.Y.Z/shellcheck-vX.Y.Z.linux.x86_64.tar.xz"
#   sha256sum /tmp/sc.tar.xz
# and paste the digest here. A stale digest fails the CI step loudly rather
# than installing something unchecked.
SHELLCHECK_SHA256=8c3be12b05d5c177a04c29e3c78ce89ac86f1595681cab149b65b97c4e227198

# yamllint checks .github/dependabot.yml, which actionlint does not read.
YAMLLINT_VERSION=1.38.0

# actionlint owns workflow semantics and runs shellcheck over every `run:`
# block. Note it therefore has a shellcheck of its OWN, bundled at build time,
# which this pin does not control — see local-ci.sh's note on that gap.
ACTIONLINT_VERSION=1.7.12

# uv resolves the dependency tree and runs pytest, so it decides more about a
# run than the three linters put together.
#
# Unlike them it cannot be INTERPOLATED into the workflow: it is installed by
# `uses: astral-sh/setup-uv` and a `uses:` input takes no shell variable. So
# the workflow repeats the literal, and tests/test_ci_contract.py asserts the
# two are equal. The test is the link that interpolation provides for the
# others — which is exactly why the pin lives here rather than only there.
UV_VERSION=0.12.2
